{"name":"Turmeric Brown","hex":"#c18116","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"turmeric","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An Indian plant (Curcuma longa), with aromatic rhizomes, part of the ginger family (Zingiberaceae).","The pulverized rhizome of the turmeric plant, used for flavoring and to add a bright yellow color to food."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turmeric"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Turmeric","blocks":[{"text":"Turmeric, or Curcuma longa, is a flowering plant in the ginger family Zingiberaceae. It is a perennial, rhizomatous, herbaceous plant native to the Indian subcontinent and Southeast Asia that requires temperatures between 20 and 30 °C and high annual rainfall to thrive. Plants are gathered each year for their rhizomes, some for propagation in the following season and some for consumption or dyeing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Turmeric_inflorescence.jpg/330px-Turmeric_inflorescence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turmeric","wikidata":"Q42562"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikiped